  "summary": "isomorphic-git allows unbounded memory allocation from attacker-controlled delta target size (DoS)",
  "details": "### Summary\nWhen applying a delta object from a packfile, isomorphic-git reads a **server-controlled** `targetSize` and calls `Buffer.alloc(targetSize)` with no upper bound. A single malicious HTTP response to `git.clone()`/`git.fetch()` can force a ~2 GB allocation → memory exhaustion / DoS (process killed on memory-constrained hosts).\n\n### Details\n`src/utils/applyDelta.js`:\n\n```js\nconst sourceSize = readVarIntLE(reader)\nconst targetSize = readVarIntLE(reader)   // attacker-controlled\n…\ntarget = Buffer.alloc(targetSize)\n```\n\nA pack with one `OBJ_REF_DELTA` whose header declares `targetSize = ",
